methods of insfiuction as well as practical work in the laboratories, hospitals, worlshopsand other govemmental or private organizations.(2) The authority responsible for organizing recognized teaching Shall be suchas may be prescribed.
C
8. cers of t e ive ity.-The following shall be the Officers ofthoUniversity:(a) Patron;(b) Chairman;(c) Rector;(d) Pro Rector;(e) Deans;(f) Chairpersons;(g) Registrar;(h) Treasurer;(i) Contoller of Examinations;(a) Director, Qualrty Enhancement Cell;(r) Director, Office of Research, Innovation and Commercialization;(k) Librarian; and(l) such other persons as may be prescribed by Regulations to be theOfficers of the University.
9. atro .{1) The Patron or his nominee shall preside over a convocation ofthe University.
(2) The Universtty may confer an honorary degree with the prior approval ofthe Patron.
. s ection a d iry.{l) The Patron may cause inspection or inquiryinto the affairs of the University.
(2) The Patron shall convey his views with regard to the result of inspection orinquiry to the Board and may, after ascertaining the views of the Board, recommendany remedial action to the Board.(3) The Board shall, within the time specified by the Patron, submit a report tothe Patron about the action taken on the recommendations of the Patron.
(4) If the Board fails to take action to the satisfaction of the Paton within thespecified time, the Patron may issue such directions as he thinks fit and the Board shallcomply with all such directions.
Provided that no action under subsection (4) shall be taken unless the Chairman ofthe Board is afforded an opportunity of being heard.
