1. C ai a .-{1) e Chairman of the Board shall be appointed by the Board ofDirectors for a renewable period of four (05) years, as the Bbard of birectors maydetermine.@ The chairman shall, preside over tho meetings ofthe Board.12. e oval o t e oard of Governor:s.{l) The Chairman may, upon therecommendation of the Review Panel, remove any person from the membership of ihe Iioard ofGovernorc on the ground that such person:(a) has beoome of unsound mind; or(b) has become incapacitated to function as member ofthe Board ofGovernors; or(c) has heen convicted by a court oflaw for an offence involvingmoral turpitude: or(d) has absented himself from two consecutive meetings withoutjust cause; or(e) has been guilty of misconduct, including use of position forpersonal advantage of any kind, or gross inefficiency in theperformance of firnctions.(2) The Chairman.shall remove any person from the membership of the Board ofGovemors on a resolution calling for the removal of such person supportid by at least eefourths of the membership ofthe Board of Governors:Provided that before passing such resolution the Board of Govemors shall provide themember concerned a fair hearing.
13. ector.{l) The Board of Directors of the company shall, on therecommendations ofthe Board, appoint a person as Rector.- (2) The Board shall constitute a Search Committee formaking recommendations forthe appointnent of Rector.(3) The Board shall determine the terms and conditions of service of the Rector.(4) The Rector shall be the person who possesses the prescribed qualifications andexperience.(5) The Rector shall perform such functions as are given in the Act or as may beprescribed or assigned to him by the Board.' rs a ties of t e ector.{l) The Rector shall be the chief executiveofficer of the University responsible for all administrative and academic functions of theUniversity and for ensuringthattheprovisions ofthe Act, Rules and Regulations are observedin all affairs ofthe University.(2) The Rector may attend a meeting of any Authority or body of the University.(3) The Rector may, in an emergency that in his opinion requires immediate
