. ea .-{1) ere shall be a Dean of each Faculty or a group of Faculties,as may be prescribed by the Act, Rulos or Regulations, who shall be the Convener of theBoard of Faoulty constituted in suoh manner as may be prescribed by the Act, Rules orRegulations.
(2) e Dean of each Faculty or a group ofFaculties shall be appointed by theBoard from amongst the t e,e senior most Professors in the Faculty or a group of Faculties,as the case may be, for such period as may be prescribed by the Board, and shall be eligiblefor re appointment:
Provided that if no Professor is available in a Faculty, a Professor from some other Facultymay act as a Dean till a Professor of the Faculty itself is appointed.
(3) e Dean shall present candidates for admission to degree, except honorarydegrees, in the courses falling within the purview of the Faculty.
(4) The Dean shall exercise such other adminishative and academic powers andperform such other functions as may be prescribed by ons.
