(a) provide shategic leadership and guidance to the University;(b) determine policy framework for invesfinent of unapplied income ofthe university in securities and acquisition of immovable property;and(c) appointment ofthe Chairman and determine the terms and oonditionsof his/her appointnent and removal;(d) In absence of Chairman of the Board, there shall be a DeputyChairman who shall be appointed on such terms and conditions asmay be prescribed by the Board of Directors. The Deputy Chairmanof the Board shall preside at the meetings of the Board and performall the functions and powers of the Chairman in his absence.(e) hire a firm of Chartered Accountants for audit of the Universityaccounts.
21. reas rer.{l) The Board shall appoint a Treasurer ofthe University.(2) The experience, professional and academic qualifications necessary for appointrnentto the post of Treasurer, method and manner of appointment as well as terms and conditionsof appoinftrent shall be as may be prescribed by Regulations.(3) The Board shall not appoint a person as Treasurer unless he possesses the prescribedqualifications and experience and other iequirements of the post.(a) The Treasurer shall be the chief financial officer of the University and shall:
(a) manage the assets, Iiabilities, receipts, expenditures, funds andinvestments of the University;(b) prepare the annual and revised budget estimates of the University andpresent the estimates to the Board;(c) ensure that the funds of the University are expended on the purposesfor which they are provided;(d) ensure that the accounts of the University are audited annually andare available for submission to the Board within six months of theclose ofa finanoial year; and(e) perform such other functions and duties as may be prescribed orassigned to him by the Rector or the Board from time to time.
(5) When the office ofthe Treasurer is vacant or the Treasurer is absent or unable to performhis functions owing to any cause, the Board shall make temporary arrangementsfor the performanoe of the duties of Treasurer.
2 . A oi t e e University may employ such other pensons in its serviceas may be necessary, on such terms and conditions as may be determined by the Board orprescribed by Regulations, as the case may be.
