23. A t ori es o t e ersi .-The following shall be the orities ofthe University:(a) Board of Governors;(b) the Executive Committee;(c) Academic Council;(d) Faculties;(e) Boards of Faculties;(f) Board of Advanced Studies and Research;(g) Boards of Studies;(h) Dep ents;(i) Selection Board;() Finance and Planning Committee;(k) Discipline Committee;(l) the Representation Committees for appointment to the Board of Govemors.the Executive Committee and the Academic Council; and(m) Such other A orities as may be prescribed by Regulations.
2 . oar of over ors.{l) The Board of Governors of the University shallconsist of the following:(a) A Director of the Company, to be nominated by the BoD, shall be theChairman of the Board;(b) Directors of the Company subjeot to a maximum of three Directors to benominated by the Company;(c) Two persons from academia and industry each one of whom is an expert in' any ofthe fields of knowledge to be nominated by the Chairman of the Board;(d) Seoretary to the Govemment, Federal Education Department or hisnominee;(e) Chairman of the Commission or his nominee;(0 A Vice Chancellor of a Federal university of Pakistan to be nominated b1'the Patron;(g) Rector ofthe University;(h) Pro-Rector of the University; and(i) Registrar (Secretary)
(7) Members of the Board other than ex-fficio members shall hold offrce for aterm of three years and shall be eligible for re-appointrnent on the explry of their termof office.(3) The quorum for a meeting of the Board shall be one-halfofthe total numberofmembers with at least two ex fficto members, a fraction being counted as one.(4) The Secretary shall, with the approval of the Chairman of the Board, call ameeting ofthe Board.
(5) In the absence of Chairman of the Board, the Deputy Chairman of the Boardshall preside at the meetings of the Board and perform all the functions and powers of'the Chairman.
lL
C A VAU S V SY

