f i a ce a ^ Ia i g com ittee.-.(r) The Finance and pranningCommittee shall consist of:
(a) Rector (Convener);(b) Alt the Deans;(c) One nominee ofthe Company;(d) one member of the Board to be nominated by the Board;(e) Director planning ofthe Commission;(0 irector, Office ofResearch, Innovation and Commercializalion;(g) Registrar; and(h) Treasurer (Secretary)(2) The members other than ex-officio members of the Finance and planningcommittee shall hold office for a term_ of three years and shall be etigible fo, ,"appoin ent on the exprry of their term of office.(3) Four members ofthe Finance and Planning Committee shall constitute the quofor a meeting ofthe Finance and planning Committee.2. ctions of t e i a ce an ra ni g co mittee.-The Finance andPlanning Committee shall :(a) prepare the annual statement of acoounts and propose annual budgetestimates and advise the Board thereon;(b) review periodically the financial position ofthe university;(c) advise the Board on all matters relating to fee ,t ,irtu ", finance,investments and accounts of the University;-and(d) perform such other functions as may be prescribed by the Regulations.43' isci Ii e Co ittee.{l) The Discipline Committee shall consist of:(a) the Convenerto be nominated by the Rector;(b) two Professors to be nominated by the Board;(c) two Associate Professors to be nominated by the Academic Counoil; and(d) the teacher or officer-in-charge of students' affairs, by whatever n*"called (Member/Secretary).(2) The members other than ex officio members of the Discipline Committee shall holdoffice for a term ofthree years and shall be eligible for re-appointnent on the expiry oftheirterm of office.
(3) The quorum for a meeting of the Discipline committee shall be fourmembers.
